                <pb facs="0158" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg62"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bryan to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Petropolis, Brazil</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1900-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November
                                30, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 290.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Complying with instructions No. 215 of
                    October 17, requesting a complete copy of the Brazilian law No. 641 of November
                    14, 1899, I have the honor to inclose herewith such copy with translation, and
                    to report that a further delay until December 31, 1900, in enforcing the
                    provisions of article 45, paragraph 2, regarding labels in Portuguese, has been
                    granted. Meanwhile the repeal or satisfactory amendment of that objectionable
                    section is definitely promised.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d51-a1.xml" xpointer="d51-a1"/>
